Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:12:28 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] EXPERIMENT: import gated PE32 x87 FIP/CS metadata from
 GUEST32-BASE

Origin: curator handoff FEX-DIRTY.diff SHA386457d86cf32d34e492fc3906b8e8e1c91d79aaf9f69d4714de91086e63f993, source HEAD0bd1d0ce8e6d68069e5d1beaff0a688e6cda300c. Existing F03 consuming-pop and F06 full-tag mechanisms agree with this handoff; imported the missing metadata path, under a separate default-OFF gate.

Family: protected-mode PE32 x87 last-instruction metadata.
Members: computational D8..DF, FNSTENV/FNSAVE16/32, FLDENV/FRSTOR16/32, FNINIT. Control operations preserve the computational FIP; init clears the ABI reserve. More than 30 computational instructions share central tracking; semantics remain separate from metadata.
Coverage: existing 8-byte CPUState reserve aliases IP/CS without changing size or following offsets (static assertions). Every metadata read/write and tracking operation requires MACRUNNER_HB_X87_FIX_FIP_CS32=1.
Not applicable to this batch: PE64 tracking, FOP/FDP/DS and FXSAVE metadata remain separate unimplemented work; no success claim for these fields.
Regression: own native shifted corpus45, all four fixes ON gives EQUAL43 plus two unchanged native CALL-address adapter faults; the nine directed F03 FNSTENV witnesses now strict EQUAL, pop control has KNOWN9. Sticky-IE control KNOWN2, tag control KNOWN16. Curator zero-restore siblings52/52 strict EQUAL. Original two-base game replay and Wine acceptance NOT_ENABLED pending low32 signing. Micro-cost manifest queued in timing FIFO, price NOT_MEASURED.
Audit completed: yes for imported metadata batch; product acceptance incomplete, no GOAL claim.
